{"availability":"available","full":"lucaperullo/simple-liquid-glass","name":"simple-liquid-glass","description":"The only zero-dependency liquid glass component with real refraction on iPhone & Safari — not a blur fallback. React 16.8–19 + web-component. ~6.5KB.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":21,"forks":1,"created":"2025-08-09T18:36:36Z","updated":"2026-09-13T17:02:12Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://glass.lucaperullo.it","topics":["apple-design","apple-liquid-glass","backdrop-filter","chromatic-aberration","frosted-glass","glass-effect","glassmorphism","ios","ios-26","liquid-glass","react","react-component","refraction","safari","ssr","svg-filter","typescript","ui-components","web-component","zero-dependency"],"demo":"https://glass.lucaperullo.it/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:44:10.143Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T16:44:10.143Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T16:44:10.143Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T16:44:10.143Z","stars":21,"forks":1}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Liquid glass for React 16.8–19, with automatic iOS WebGL refraction, optional Android WebGL, and SVG optics.","An Apple-style glass effect with displacement, chromatic aberration, gradient borders, and automatic text color. Includes an optional interactive component and a framework-agnostic web component. Server-rendering and hydration are tested alongside browser behavior.","For WebGL refraction on iOS (or any platform with renderer=\"webgl\"), use LiquidGlassScene or pass backdropRef pointing to a sibling background element. Without either source the component uses frosted CSS."],"features":["No additional renderer installation: WebGL and HTML capture are bundled. React is a peer dependency for React entry points.","Automatic WebGL refraction on iOS; opt into it on Android or desktop with renderer=\"webgl\". Chromium SVG and desktop Safari/Firefox mirrors remain available.","React 16.8–19 compatibility checked with server rendering, hydration, and unmount tests.","A separate web component for other frameworks, with the same iOS WebGL engine.","Enforced bundle budgets and browser integration tests in Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lucaperullo/simple-liquid-glass/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"ab6da9b8ab19610d4afec255ce54bd0babe486ae2850bb3d3a3a14947b81f3a6","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T16:44:10.255Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:44:10.255Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Liquid glass for React 16.8–19, with automatic iOS WebGL refraction, optional Android WebGL, and SVG optics.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lucaperullo/simple-liquid-glass/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"ab6da9b8ab19610d4afec255ce54bd0babe486ae2850bb3d3a3a14947b81f3a6","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lucaperullo/simple-liquid-glass/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T16:44:10.255Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-13T17:02:12Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lucaperullo/simple-liquid-glass/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T16:44:10.257Z","hash":"ab6da9b8ab19610d4afec255ce54bd0babe486ae2850bb3d3a3a14947b81f3a6","originalBytes":35005,"storedBytes":35005,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["webgl","react","svg","glass","blur","css","renderer","background","uses","import","component","npm","simple-liquid-glass","effect","html","ios","color","capture","content","lens","refraction","run","default","displacement","quality","source","when","backdrop","safari","desktop","firefox","number","preset","text","web","liquid","mirror","scale","strength","browser","jsx","material","auto","chromium","dispersion","existing","explicit","fallback","gradient","performance","support","automatically","border","changes","only","page","saturation","android","automatic","backdropref","canvas","chromatic","css-only","custom","ef